 "level_notes": {"1": "No standard (the 1993 ANSI Object-Oriented Extensions to Pascal draft was never adopted). Delphi is defined by Embarcadero's Delphi Language Guide (docwiki, which refuses automated clients and reports 'blocked'); Free Pascal's Reference Guide documents its modes (fpc, objfpc, delphi, tp, macpas, iso) and is linked section by section here.", "0": "Free Pascal (self-hosted, written in Object Pascal) lives on GitLab (freepascal.org/fpc/source); Delphi's compiler is proprietary, though its RTL/VCL source ships with the product. Lazarus is the FPC-based IDE and LCL component library."},
